From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wayland/touch: reject grabs from cancelled touch sequences

meta_wayland_touch_cancel() clears focus_surface but retains the touch
sequence until its end event. A client can still submit the old serial
to request an interactive move or resize during that interval.

Reject that request instead of dereferencing the cleared focus_surface.
Two Piano crash dumps from Mutter 51.0 show a NULL first member of
MetaWaylandTouchInfo at touch_can_grab_surface(). The same unchecked
dereference is present in upstream 51.1.
---
diff --git a/src/wayland/meta-wayland-touch.c b/src/wayland/meta-wayland-touch.c
--- a/src/wayland/meta-wayland-touch.c
+++ b/src/wayland/meta-wayland-touch.c
@@ -659,6 +659,10 @@ touch_can_grab_surface (MetaWaylandTouchInfo *touch_info,
 {
   MetaWaylandSurface *subsurface;
 
+  /* Cancellation drops focus before the sequence's end event arrives. */
+  if (!touch_info->focus_surface)
+    return FALSE;
+
   if (touch_info->focus_surface->surface == surface)
     return TRUE;
 
